[
  {
    "id": 279330,
    "name": "Diamond Ray of Disappearance",
    "season": 1,
    "number": 1,
    "type": "regular",
    "airdate": "1983-09-05",
    "runtime": 30,
    "summary": "<p>At Snake Mountain Skeletor commands Beast Man to activate the transport beam. Within moments Evil-Lyn, Mer-Man, Trap Jaw, and Tri-Klops all appear. Skeletor reveals that the Diamond of Disappearance is now in his possession, a gem that transports whoever is looking at it into another dimension.</p>"
  },
  {
    "id": 279331,
    "name": "Teela's Quest",
    "season": 1,
    "number": 2,
    "type": "regular",
    "airdate": "1983-09-06",
    "runtime": 30,
    "summary": "<p>Teela's desire to find out who her mother is sets her on adventure into Crystal Sea region to find the Oracle. But Crystal Sea is home territory of Mer-Man and he has another plan in mind... to enact vengeance on Man-at-Arms who 20 years ago rescued a victim intended as a sacrifice for the sea demon Bakkull. Now, Mer-Man's plan is to capture Teela and sacrifice her to Bakkull. His plan comes to a halt when He-Man comes to a rescue.</p>"
  },
  {
    "id": 279332,
    "name": "Colossor Awakes",
    "season": 1,
    "number": 3,
    "type": "regular",
    "airdate": "1983-09-07",
    "runtime": 30,
    "summary": "<p>Skeletor uses his new attack ship, the Collector, to turn people into stone and stone statues to his allies. He-Man stops his attack on the castle, but not before he turns Man-at-Arms into stone. But Skeletor always plans big, and his next step is to use a device called the Energizer to bring the gigantic stone statue of Colossor to life.</p>"
  },
  {
    "id": 279333,
    "name": "The Dragon Invasion",
    "season": 1,
    "number": 4,
    "type": "regular",
    "airdate": "1983-09-08",
    "runtime": 30,
    "summary": "<p>At Dragonmount, Skeletor and Beast Man steal several of the Mother Dragon's eggs. Skeletor explains to Best Man that he is now in possession of the powerful Dragonpearl. With dragons under the control of Beast Man creating havoc across all of Eternia, Skeletor and Evil-Lyn head on to take castle Grayskull, capturing the Sorceress inside the Dragonpearls.</p>"
  },
  {
    "id": 279334,
    "name": "The Curse of the Spellstone",
    "season": 1,
    "number": 5,
    "type": "regular",
    "airdate": "1983-09-09",
    "runtime": 30,
    "summary": "<p>Skeletor and Evil-Lyn invade the temple of Fire People in order to take possession of the Spellstone, a special orb that can control weather. Skeletor uses it to provoke conflict and Evil-Lyn to turn the villagers against king Randor, throwing the Creeping Horak at the palace as a form of punishment. While king and queen, accompanies by Teela, Man-at-Arms and Orko try to find a way to stop the Creeping Horak, He-Man and Stratoss try to find the Spellstone and use it to rescue everyone at the palace and return it to the Fire People.</p>"
  },
